309 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 131 0 R
/E (A key point of the consultation discussions was the recognition of the importance of changing PoSH implementation from a mere compliance measure into a governance function. It became evident that while a vast majority of organisations have developed policies and formed internal committees as per the Sexual Harassment of Women at Workplace \(Prevention, Prohibition and Redressal\), Act, 2013 \(PoSH 2013\), implementation remained procedural rather than strategic. The discussions revealed that the process of creating a safe workplace goes beyond just paperwork and involves ensuring leadership buy-in, accountability at the institutional level, and establishing systems that can prevent, detect, and react to any wrongdoings in the organisation. The consultation called for shifting from a compliance-driven approach to a capability-based approach centred on developing organisational capabilities. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
