313 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 131 0 R
/T ( 2. Closing the gap between policy and practice)
/E ( 2. Closing the gap between policy and practice)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
314 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 131 0 R
/E (Participants also noted the increasing gap between well-written PoSH policies and their implementation in organisations. The issue here is whether the continuously emerging automated and standardised policies are truly relevant for organisations or whether they are merely a symbol of compliance. Among the main reasons for failure of implementation, participants mentioned lack of awareness, inconsistent approach, insufficient training for Internal Committees, and weak leadership.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
315 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 131 0 R
/T ( 3. Strengthening the effectiveness of the Internal Committee)
/E ( 3. Strengthening the effectiveness of the Internal Committee)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
316 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 131 0 R
/E (The consultation underscored the crucial role of the Internal Committee in the PoSH architecture and pointed out the issues associated with uniformity, neutrality, and legal readiness. Discussions revolved around challenging inquiries, documentation requirements, workplace relations, and the tension between confidentiality and fairness. Overall, the consultation made it clear that capacity development, practical exercises, and process reviews must be ongoing.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
317 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 131 0 R
/T ( 4. Anonymous complaints, retaliation, and trust in the Organisation)
/E ( 4. Anonymous complaints, retaliation, and trust in the Organisation)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
318 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 131 0 R
/E (The discussion focused on anonymous complaints and the circumstances that create them. Participants asked whether anonymous complaints could be lodged within existing legislation and how to balance the need for natural justice with organisational accountability. Another point made was concerns about retaliatory measures; hierarchy in the organisation, performance evaluation, and power imbalance. These constitute an obstacle to reporting cases and therefore need to be addressed through the introduction of stronger whistleblower rights and mechanisms not allowing for retaliation.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
