334 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 132 0 R
/T (1. Mere compliance is not enough to ensure workplace safety)
/E (1. Mere compliance is not enough to ensure workplace safety)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
335 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 132 0 R
/E (Participants agreed that compliance is just a necessary base for any organisation to fulfil its legal responsibility. Policies, internal committees, and obligatory training are not enough for the proper implementation of their responsibilities. The real safety at the workplace relies on the organisational culture, leadership undertakings, correct procedures, and constant organisational learning.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
336 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 132 0 R
/T (2. Leadership accountability is important for PoSH governance )
/E (2. Leadership accountability is important for PoSH governance )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
337 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 132 0 R
/E (One important idea that emerged from the discussion was that responsibility for workplace safety does not rest solely with the Internal Committee or the HR department. The top managers and leaders of the organisation play key roles in shaping the workplace culture, providing the resources, and making the decisions. PoSH should be dealt with at the level of governance. It requires organisation-wide ownership, with leadership, managers, and employees all playing an active role in fostering a safe and respectful workplace. )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
