588 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 146 0 R
/T (Some of the key reflections emerging during the consultation were as follows:)
/E (Some of the key reflections emerging during the consultation were as follows:)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
589 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 146 0 R
/E (Employees need to be made fully aware of their rights and obligations under the PoSH Act. Issues such as confidentiality, non-retaliation / victimisation and handling of grievances leave a lasting impact on the employees participating in a process and shape the environment of the organisation.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
590 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 146 0 R
/E (The involvement of leaders in PoSH implementation is one of the surest indicators of success. )
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
591 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 146 0 R
/E (Harassment \(including sexual harassment\) and bullying are more often than not a trickle-down issue, managers / supervisors need to be equally made aware of their role in maintaining a harassment free environment.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
592 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 146 0 R
/E (Anonymous complaints point to some deeper issues in relation to the trust in the organisation or its psychological safety.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
593 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 146 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
594 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 146 0 R
/E (Frequent organisational reviews coupled with data-based assessments allow for discovering systemic issues before they become more serious and lead to any formal disagreements.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
