629 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 148 0 R
/E (Anumita Sarkar is an Independent Policy and Strategic Advisor and Founder of P/ PRABHAVEE, a Delhi-based strategy consulting practice working at the intersection of policy, law, and business strategy. She specialises in social sustainability, labour rights, governance, ethics and compliance, business integrity, corporate accountability, human rights, and responsible business. Through strategic advisory, multi-stakeholder consultations, training and capacity-building, and other strategic engagements and programmes, she advises organisations on embedding responsible business practices and strengthening governance frameworks.)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
630 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 148 0 R
/E (A strategic leader with an interdisciplinary academic background in Sociology, Law, Communications, and Strategic Management, Anumita brings close to 20 years of cross-sectoral, cross-functional, and multi-stakeholder experience. Her work spans regulatory risk consulting, legal and compliance, public policy, social impact, academia, and responsible business, with expertise in translating complex regulatory and governance challenges into practical organisational strategies. She has worked across diverse sectors, including legal technology \(GRC\), publishing and information services, consulting, higher education, public policy, social enterprise, nonprofit accelerator, and advisory boards. Throughout her career, she has collaborated extensively with government institutions, the private sector, nonprofits, industry associations, business chambers, academia, think tanks, and C-suite leaders. Prior to her work in Consulting, Anumita spent over 11 years in tax practice, legal technology, publishing, and information services, building a strong foundation in governance, risk management, and business operations. )
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
631 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 148 0 R
/E (Anumita started her career as a litigator specialising in tax matters and spent 5 years in litigation. She appeared before quasi-judicial authorities, Tax Tribunals in Delhi and Kolkata, represented before government authorities and various forums, and has independently handled matters, achieving several favourable judgments. She later moved on to work for a legal technology company. Anumita has spent approximately 7 years in the legal technology and information services sector, with expertise spanning regulatory compliance, governance, risk, and compliance solutions, and product management, working on digital software and knowledge-based products.)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
632 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 148 0 R
/E (Anumita is recognised for building strategic partnerships and designing high-impact capacity-building programmes. She delivers lectures and professional training on sustainability and the social dimensions of ESG and responsible business. She advises organisations on multi-stakeholder initiatives, facilitates strategic consultations, develops knowledge partnerships, and designs learning programmes that strengthen governance and organisational capability. Anumita is a Prevention of Sexual Harassment of Women at the Workplace \(PoSH\) advisor registered with the Ministry of Women & Child Development, Government of India. She serves as an External Member of PoSH Internal Committees and is an Advisory Board Member of a grassroots non-governmental organisation.)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
633 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 148 0 R
/E (She is a strategic partner to Higher Educational Institutions, Universities, Academic Research Centres, Think Tanks, Policy Research and Advocacy Organisations. She currently collaborates with the Centre for Business and Human Rights \(CBHR\) at Tamil Nadu National Law University. )
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
634 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 148 0 R
/E (Anumita is an alumna of Miranda House College and Campus Law Centre, Faculty of Law, University of Delhi, Cohort 5 alumna of the Women on Boards Programme at the Indian School of Development Management \(ISDM\), and an alumni member of the International Training Centre of the ILO \(ITCILO\).)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [7]
>>
